
==========================================================================
  EXAMPLE A — a token built to be exited
==========================================================================
  [CRITICAL]  UNCAPPED MINT
     The team can create new tokens at will. Your share can be diluted to nothing,
     and the new supply can be dumped on the pool you are holding.

  [CRITICAL]  SELL BLOCK / HONEYPOT
     A per-address or global switch on selling. You can buy, and then find you
     are the only one who cannot get out. This is what a honeypot is.

  [CRITICAL]  UNBOUNDED FEE
     A fee the owner can change with no upper bound written into the code.
     A 100% sell tax is a rug that does not even need to move the liquidity.

  [CRITICAL]  OWNER CAN PULL LIQUIDITY
     The team can take the trading pool itself. The token still exists;
     there is simply nothing left to sell it into.


  -> 4 red flag(s).

==========================================================================
  EXAMPLE B — the same functions, bounded
==========================================================================
  [    good]  renounceOwnership
  [    good]  hard-capped supply

  -> no red flags in these five patterns.
